rules.content_en:
####### Rule Overview
This rule aims to detect whether the parameter types passed to the `scanf` function match the expected format specifiers.

######## Significance of the Rule
Passing mismatched parameter types may lead to undefined behavior or program crashes; ensuring that parameter types are consistent with format specifiers is an important aspect of safe programming.

######## Error Example
```c
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    int value;
    // Error: A float type variable is passed, but %d format specifier is used
