    int result = ptr + offset; // 正确：在进行运算前检查指针
}
```

rules.content_en:
####### Rule Overview
When performing pointer arithmetic, involving a null pointer will lead to undefined behavior. This rule requires checking and avoiding unnecessary null pointer arithmetic.

######## Rule Significance
Undefined behavior during pointer addition or subtraction can cause program crashes or instability. Ensuring that pointers are validated before arithmetic operations can enhance the safety and stability of the code.

######## Error Example
```cpp
int* ptr = nullptr;
int offset = 5;
int result = ptr + offset; // Error: arithmetic operation on a null pointer
```

