rules.content:
####### 规则概述
在使用 `InterlockedDecrement` 函数之后，可能存在对同一变量的不安全访问。这可能导致竞态条件，从而引发未定义行为。

######## 规则意义
该规则用于检测在多线程环境中，代码在使用 `InterlockedDecrement` 后是否有其他线程对同一资源的访问，从而避免由于不同线程的操作顺序导致的数据不一致和潜在的崩溃。

######## 错误示例
'''cpp
#include <windows.h>
#include <iostream>

int globalVar = 0;

DWORD WINAPI threadFunc(LPVOID lpParam) {
    InterlockedDecrement(&globalVar);
    // 此处对 globalVar 的使用可能会导致竞态条件
    std::cout << globalVar << std::endl;
    return 0;
}

int main() {
    HANDLE threads[2];
    for (int i = 0; i < 2; i++) {
        threads[i] = CreateThread(NULL, 0, threadFunc, NULL, 0, NULL);
    }
    WaitForMultipleObjects(2, threads, TRUE, INFINITE);
    return 0;
}
'''

######## 正确示例
'''cpp
#include <windows.h>
#include <iostream>
#include <mutex>

int globalVar = 0;
std::mutex mtx;

DWORD WINAPI threadFunc(LPVOID lpParam) {
    InterlockedDecrement(&globalVar);
    // 使用互斥锁保证对 globalVar 的安全访问
    mtx.lock();
    std::cout << globalVar << std::endl;
    mtx.unlock();
    return 0;
}

int main() {
    HANDLE threads[2];
    for (int i = 0; i < 2; i++) {
        threads[i] = CreateThread(NULL, 0, threadFunc, NULL, 0, NULL);
    }
    WaitForMultipleObjects(2, threads, TRUE, INFINITE);
    return 0;
}
'''

rules.content_en:
####### Rule Overview
After using the `InterlockedDecrement` function, there may be unsafe access to the same variable. This can lead to race conditions, resulting in undefined behavior.

######## Rule Meaning
This rule is used to detect in a multithreaded environment whether other threads access the same resource after using `InterlockedDecrement`, thus avoiding data inconsistency and potential crashes due to the operational order of different threads.

######## Error Example
'''cpp
#include <windows.h>
#include <iostream>

int globalVar = 0;

DWORD WINAPI threadFunc(LPVOID lpParam) {
    InterlockedDecrement(&globalVar);
    // Accessing globalVar here may lead to a race condition
    std::cout << globalVar << std::endl;
    return 0;
}

int main() {
    HANDLE threads[2];
    for (int i = 0; i < 2; i++) {
        threads[i] = CreateThread(NULL, 0, threadFunc, NULL, 0, NULL);
    }
    WaitForMultipleObjects(2, threads, TRUE, INFINITE);
    return 0;
}
'''

######## Correct Example
'''cpp
#include <windows.h>
#include <iostream>
#include <mutex>

int globalVar = 0;
std::mutex mtx;

DWORD WINAPI threadFunc(LPVOID lpParam) {
    InterlockedDecrement(&globalVar);
    // Use a mutex to ensure safe access to globalVar
    mtx.lock();
    std::cout << globalVar << std::endl;
    mtx.unlock();
    return 0;
}

int main() {
    HANDLE threads[2];
    for (int i = 0; i < 2; i++) {
        threads[i] = CreateThread(NULL, 0, threadFunc, NULL, 0, NULL);
    }
    WaitForMultipleObjects(2, threads, TRUE, INFINITE);
    return 0;
}
'''

rules.content:
####### 规则概述
此规则旨在确保程序只对其拥有写权限的文件执行写操作，以防止潜在的数据丢失或安全问题。

######## 规则意义
在进行文件操作时，确保文件的读写权限设置是良好的编程实践。错误地对没有写权限的文件进行写操作可能导致运行时错误或数据丢失。

######## 错误示例
'''cpp
#include <fstream>

void writeFile(const std::string& filepath) {
    std::ofstream ofs(filepath);
    ofs << "This will fail if the file is read-only.";
    ofs.close();
}
'''

######## 正确示例
'''cpp
#include <fstream>
#include <sys/stat.h>

void writeFile(const std::string& filepath) {
    struct stat buf;
    if (stat(filepath.c_str(), &buf) == 0 && (buf.st_mode & S_IWUSR)) {
        std::ofstream ofs(filepath);
        ofs << "This will succeed if the file is writable.";
        ofs.close();
    } else {
        std::cerr << "File is read-only or doesn't exist.";
    }
}
'''

rules.content_en:
####### Rule Overview
This rule aims to ensure that the program only performs write operations on files it has write permissions for, preventing potential data loss or security issues.

######## Significance of the Rule
When performing file operations, ensuring that the read and write permissions of the file are correctly set is a good programming practice. Incorrectly writing to a file without write permissions may lead to runtime errors or data loss.

######## Error Example
'''cpp
#include <fstream>

void writeFile(const std::string& filepath) {
    std::ofstream ofs(filepath);
    ofs << "This will fail if the file is read-only.";
    ofs.close();
}
'''

######## Correct Example
'''cpp
#include <fstream>
#include <sys/stat.h>

void writeFile(const std::string& filepath) {
    struct stat buf;
    if (stat(filepath.c_str(), &buf) == 0 && (buf.st_mode & S_IWUSR)) {
        std::ofstream ofs(filepath);
        ofs << "This will succeed if the file is writable.";
        ofs.close();
    } else {
        std::cerr << "File is read-only or doesn't exist.";
    }
}
'''

rules.content:
####### 规则概述
在switch语句中的case分支中，重复赋值给同一个变量可能会导致不必要的代码复杂性和潜在的逻辑错误。

######## 规则意义
确保代码简洁性和可维护性，避免逻辑混淆和不必要的冗余赋值。

######## 错误示例
```cpp
int value = 0;
switch (someCondition) {
    case 1:
        value = 5;
        break;
    case 2:
        value = 5; // 冗余赋值
        break;
}
```

######## 正确示例
```cpp
int value = 0;
switch (someCondition) {
    case 1:
        value = 5;
        break;
    case 2:
        break;
}
```

rules.content_en:
####### Rule Overview
In the case branches of a switch statement, repeatedly assigning a value to the same variable may lead to unnecessary code complexity and potential logical errors.

######## Rule Significance
Ensures code simplicity and maintainability, avoiding logical confusion and unnecessary redundant assignments.

######## Error Example
```cpp
int value = 0;
switch (someCondition) {
    case 1:
        value = 5;
        break;
    case 2:
        value = 5; // Redundant assignment
        break;
}
```

######## Correct Example
```cpp
int value = 0;
switch (someCondition) {
    case 1:
        value = 5;
        break;
    case 2:
        break;
}
```

rules.content:
####### 规则概述
