rules.content:
####### 规则概述
该规则用于检查C++ STL容器的大小是否在使用过程中保持一致，以避免潜在的逻辑错误。

######## 规则意义
在使用 STL 容器时，容器的大小应当在适当的情况下保持一致。如果容器的大小发生变化而未及时更新相关的逻辑，可能导致程序出现未定义行为或逻辑错误。

######## 错误示例
```cpp
#include <vector>
#include <iostream>

int main() {
    std::vector<int> vec;
    vec.push_back(1);
    vec.push_back(2);
    // 假设这里需要使用 vec.size() 来判断循环次数，但可能会有意外的逻辑错误
    if (vec.size() == 2) {
        std::cout << "Size is 2" << std::endl;
    }
    vec.pop_back(); // 此时 vec.size() 变为 1
    // 错误的假设：继续依赖 vec.size() 的值
    std::cout << "Size is still 2" << std::endl; // 逻辑错误！
}
```

######## 正确示例
```cpp
#include <vector>
#include <iostream>

int main() {
    std::vector<int> vec;
    vec.push_back(1);
    vec.push_back(2);
    // 使用大小前需要确认是否有变更
    size_t size = vec.size();
    if (size == 2) {
        std::cout << "Size is 2" << std::endl;
    }
    vec.pop_back();
    // 正确处理容器大小的变化
    size = vec.size();
    std::cout << "Updated size: " << size << std::endl; // 输出应为 1
}
```

rules.content_en:
####### Rule Overview
This rule is used to check whether the size of C++ STL containers remains consistent during usage, in order to avoid potential logical errors.

######## Rule Significance
When using STL containers, the size of the container should remain consistent under appropriate circumstances. If the size of the container changes and the related logic is not updated in a timely manner, it may lead to undefined behavior or logical errors in the program.

######## Error Example
```cpp
#include <vector>
#include <iostream>

int main() {
    std::vector<int> vec;
    vec.push_back(1);
    vec.push_back(2);
    // Assume that vec.size() needs to be used to determine the number of iterations, but there may be unexpected logical errors
    if (vec.size() == 2) {
        std::cout << "Size is 2" << std::endl;
    }
    vec.pop_back(); // At this point vec.size() becomes 1
    // Incorrect assumption: continuing to rely on the value of vec.size()
    std::cout << "Size is still 2" << std::endl; // Logical error!
}
```

######## Correct Example
```cpp
#include <vector>
#include <iostream>

int main() {
    std::vector<int> vec;
    vec.push_back(1);
    vec.push_back(2);
    // Confirm if there's any change before using the size
    size_t size = vec.size();
    if (size == 2) {
        std::cout << "Size is 2" << std::endl;
    }
    vec.pop_back();
    // Properly handle changes in the container size
    size = vec.size();
    std::cout << "Updated size: " << size << std::endl; // Output should be 1
}
```

