    return 0;
}
```

rules.content_en:
####### Rule Overview
This rule detects cases where a variable is used before it has been assigned a value.

######## Rule Meaning
Uninitialized variables can lead to unpredictable behavior, causing errors during program execution, which may result in crashes or other serious consequences. Therefore, ensuring that all variables are properly assigned before use is good programming practice.

