rules.content:
####### 规则概述
在C/C++中，函数应当能够妥善处理可能发生的异常，以避免未定义的行为和程序崩溃。

######## 规则意义
处理异常规定可以确保程序在出现错误时依然能够保持稳定，并有效提升程序的可靠性和健壮性。

######## 错误示例
'''cpp
#include <iostream>

void riskyFunction() throw() {
    throw std::runtime_error("Something went wrong"); // 抛出了异常但是未处理
}

int main() {
    try {
        riskyFunction();
    } catch (const std::exception& e) {
        std::cerr << "Error: " << e.what() << '\n';
    }
    return 0;
}
''''

######## 正确示例
'''cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <exception>

void riskyFunction() throw() {
    throw std::runtime_error("Something went wrong"); // 确保在调用处处理异常
}

int main() {
    try {
        riskyFunction();
    } catch (const std::exception& e) {
        std::cerr << "Handled Error: " << e.what() << '\n';
    }
    return 0;
}
''''

rules.content_en:
####### Rule Overview
In C/C++, functions should be able to properly handle potential exceptions to avoid undefined behavior and program crashes.

######## Rule Significance
Exception handling stipulations ensure that programs can remain stable in the face of errors, effectively enhancing the reliability and robustness of the program.

######## Error Example
'''cpp
#include <iostream>

void riskyFunction() throw() {
    throw std::runtime_error("Something went wrong"); // An exception is thrown but not handled
}

int main() {
    try {
        riskyFunction();
    } catch (const std::exception& e) {
        std::cerr << "Error: " << e.what() << '\n';
    }
    return 0;
}
''''

######## Correct Example
'''cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <exception>

void riskyFunction() throw() {
    throw std::runtime_error("Something went wrong"); // Ensure the exception is handled at the call site
}

int main() {
    try {
        riskyFunction();
    } catch (const std::exception& e) {
        std::cerr << "Handled Error: " << e.what() << '\n';
    }
    return 0;
}
''''

