rules.content:
####### 规则概述
此规则检查代码中是否存在对已关闭文件的访问。这可能导致未定义行为或程序崩溃。

######## 规则意义
在文件操作中，确保文件在被操作时是处于打开状态是非常重要的。如果试图在文件关闭后对其进行读写，可能会引发严重的错误或数据丢失。

######## 错误示例
```cpp
#include <fstream>

void Example() {
    std::ifstream file("example.txt");
    file.close();  // 关闭文件
    char buffer[100];
    file.getline(buffer, 100);  // 尝试读取已关闭的文件
}
```

######## 正确示例
```cpp
#include <fstream>

void Example() {
    std::ifstream file("example.txt");
    char buffer[100];
    if (file.is_open()) {
        file.getline(buffer, 100);  // 安全访问已打开的文件
    }
    file.close();  // 关闭文件
}
```

rules.content_en:
####### Rule Overview
This rule checks for attempts to access a closed file in the code. This may lead to undefined behavior or program crashes.

######## Rule Significance
It is crucial to ensure that a file is in an open state while performing file operations. Attempting to read from or write to a file after it has been closed can result in severe errors or data loss.

######## Error Example
```cpp
#include <fstream>

void Example() {
    std::ifstream file("example.txt");
    file.close();  // Close the file
    char buffer[100];
    file.getline(buffer, 100);  // Attempt to read from a closed file
}
```

######## Correct Example
```cpp
#include <fstream>

void Example() {
    std::ifstream file("example.txt");
    char buffer[100];
    if (file.is_open()) {
        file.getline(buffer, 100);  // Safely access the opened file
    }
    file.close();  // Close the file
}
```

