In C/C++ development, the functionality provided by the standard library should be prioritized to improve code readability, maintainability, and performance.

######## Rule Significance
Using the standard library helps avoid reinventing the wheel, reduces the amount of code, and the implementations of the standard library are extensively tested and optimized, enhancing the stability and performance of the program. Utilizing the standard library also contributes to code consistency and readability. To ensure code quality, developers are encouraged to use the features provided by the standard library whenever feasible.

