}
```

rules.content_en:
####### Rule Overview
This rule aims to detect improper usage of `va_start`. When a reference type variable is passed as a function parameter, it may lead to incorrect `va_start` calls.

######## Significance of the Rule
Incorrect use of `va_start` can result in abnormal program behavior or crashes, as it may fail to obtain the correct value on the stack. Ensure that only basic types are passed when using variable-length arguments.

######## Error Example
```cpp
#include <cstdarg>

void example(int& count, ...){
    va_list args;
    va_start(args, count);
